# Keep secrets and bulk out of the build context.
#
# EVERY pattern here uses **/ deliberately. Docker ignore globs use
# filepath.Match and `*` NEVER crosses a `/`, so a bare `.env` matches the
# repo-root file and nothing else -- not .env.local, not institutions/.env.
# The project's own pre-commit hook already treats `.env.*` and `*/.env` as
# the threat surface, so those files are real here.
#
# This matters more than the rest of the file: an image is pushed to ECR, and
# a key baked into a layer is NOT removed by deleting the file in a later one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!.env.example

**/.venv/
**/venv/
.git/
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Not needed at runtime. Tests stay OUT: they pull in nothing the image needs
# and only widen what ships.
tests/
docs/
demo/
eval/
*.md
!README.md
